    "description": "Accomplishments/Responsibilities\n•\tActing Team Lead for two Clients, Ocwen (1/2 year) and Well Fargo (3 years). Responsible for all development work on client projects and making deadlines or milestones. Teams I was in charge of ranged from 1 to 10 people. I would manage resources work, along with develop code, create technical specs, design solution, help in deployment, code reviews, and training if needed. I also would work with Business Analysts on Customer specifications, along with giving LOEs to project managers for what it would take to do a project.\n•\tWorked on large ColdFusion application which our Lenders, Vendors, and Agents would interface with in order to conduct their business. (Our web system was built on ColdFusion 9, ColdBox, SQL Server, Query, JavaScript, SSIS, and Java). I was the main ColdFusion developer on all the Wells Fargo Short Sale Application pieces.\n•\tProjects would go through formal SDLC process (Dev-QA-Beta(client)-Stage-Production), which I would have to help at all stages to have successful deployments. Code was put in MKS Integrity.\n•\tI was part of implementation of many large projects (over 300 hours) for Wells Fargo (FHA Workflow, Single Sign On, FileNet/ICMP Integration, Wells Owned/FHA Workflow, Load Balancing, SSDT, Closing, and Low Docs workflow).\n•\tImplement 200+ Bug CRs (under 50 hrs projects) for clients that included (Wells, Ocwen, Chase, Bank of America, Fannie Mae, Carrington, and others)\n•\tEarn two performance awards in 2010 for department, before it was discontinued.",
